  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "If the area of the triangle whose one vertex is at the vertex of the parabola, $y^{2}+4\\left(x-a^{2}\\right)=0$ and the other two vertices are the points of intersection of the parabola and $y$ -axis, is 250 sq. units, then a value of 'a' is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "lOzBS",
      "text": "$5 \\sqrt{5}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "DwS0k",
      "text": "$5\\left(2^{1 / 3}\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "iTn4r",
      "text": "$(10)^{33}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "G3Bw8",
      "text": "5",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$y^{t}=-4\\left(x-a^{2}\\right)$\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/0pFWq6xYy6euRwfWHifO2c-ZqETw7H3Bt9DZMpw2PCI.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{Area}=\\frac{1}{2}(4 a)\\left(a^{2}\\right)=2 a^{3}$\r\n\r\nSince $2 a^{3}=250 \\Rightarrow a=5$",
    "image": null
  },
